+
+\subsection{One Independent Sequential Witness}
+
+Let $\eta$ be the causal enumeration supplied by
+Theorem~\ref{thm:rga-representation}. Form $\pi$ by listing its insertions in
+increasing identifier order, followed by its deletions. The order among the
+deletions does not affect the argument. This word enumerates exactly the same
+original events.
+
+Every insertion's original anchor birth has a smaller identifier and therefore
+appears earlier. No deletion has yet removed that anchor, so the insertion-first
+prefix has live anchors and satisfies the sequential specification's guards.
+Every deletion has its birth in that prefix. A concrete fold lemma identifies
+the records present after any well-formed fold: they are precisely the original
+insertion records whose identifiers are never deleted in the word. Sortedness
+then fixes their list order. It follows that $\pi(\sigma_0)=\eta(\sigma_0)=s$
+as entire concrete states, not just as query answers.
+
+The same word respects $\F{lo}^{C,I_C}_E$. On supported events its only possible
+implementation-conflicting visibility edges run from a birth to deletion of
+that birth; insertions precede deletions in $\pi$. Independent specification
+visibility is a separate obligation. The history proof establishes contextual
+commutation for the pairs involving a deletion that $\pi$ moves, using both admission and
+subsequent abstract behavior, and preserves all remaining specified conflicts.
+Thus it proves the two order properties and admission for one word.
+
+\begin{theorem}[Embedded-RGA independent history]
+\label{thm:rga-history}
+Under the hypotheses of Theorem~\ref{thm:rga-representation}, for every
+allocated version $S(v)=(s,E)$ there is an enumeration $\pi$ of $E$ such that
+\[
+\begin{gathered}
+ \pi\text{ respects }\F{lo}^{C,I_C}_E
+ \text{ and specification-conflict visibility},\\
+ \pi(\sigma_0)=s,\qquad
+ \forall q\in Q_\tau.\
+ \F{ops}_{\mathrm{id}}(\pi)\cdot
+ (q\Rightarrow\mathcal D_\tau.\F{query}(s,q))\in\Spec.
+\end{gathered}
+\]
+The original full-event specification and original public query are unchanged.
+\end{theorem}
+
+\noindent\emph{Proof.}
+Use the insertion-first word just constructed. Original issuance and causal
+support establish its sequential legality. The well-formed fold lemma proves
+its exact reconstruction, and the two order arguments preserve the required
+conflicts. The independent list refinement relates its concrete record list
+to its abstract tagged list; projecting their values gives the query answer.
+The certified exact-witness lifting theorem
+(Theorem~\ref{thm:certified-lift}) then establishes the per-version criterion.
+Apply the argument at each visited configuration for the finite-execution
+claim.\hfill$\square$
